  "text": {
    "markdown": "## Which phone plan for 12 GB a month and two weeks abroad?\n\n**Recommendation: Plus.** It covers 12 GB with room to spare and costs **$550 a year** including roaming, against $720 for Max. Basic is the most expensive of the three for this usage and does not work abroad at all.\n\n| | Basic | **Plus** | Max |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Monthly price | $25 | $40 | $60 |\n| Data included | 5 GB | 20 GB | Unlimited |\n| Extra data | $10 per GB | — | — |\n| Roaming | Not available | $5 per day | Included |\n| **Monthly cost at 12 GB** | **$95** | **$40** | **$60** |\n| Roaming for 14 days | Not possible | $70 | $0 |\n| **Cost per year** | **$1,140** + no service abroad | **$550** | **$720** |\n\n### How the numbers work out\n\n- **Basic:** you would use 7 GB over the 5 GB allowance. 7 × $10 = $70 in overage, so $25 becomes **$95 a month**, or $1,140 a year. And there is no roaming for the two trips.\n- **Plus:** 12 GB fits inside 20 GB, so it stays at $40 a month, $480 a year. Two one-week trips are 14 roaming days × $5 = $70. Total **$550**.\n- **Max:** $60 × 12 = **$720**, with data and roaming included.\n\nPlus saves **$170 a year** over Max and **$590** over Basic.\n\n### When the answer would change\n\n- **Choose Max** if you spend more than **48 days a year** abroad (48 × $5 = $240, the price gap between Plus and Max), or if your usage grows past 20 GB a month.\n- **Choose Basic** only if you use 5 GB or less and never travel. It becomes more expensive than Plus as soon as you pass 6.5 GB a month.\n",
    "validation": {
      "valid": true,
      "checks": [
        "is non-empty Markdown",
        "contains no raw HTML outside code (react-markdown would print it literally)"
      ],
      "errors": [],
      "warnings": []
    }
  },
